            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial hypertension and levofloxacin: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2008.01212.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of a 15-year-old boy who developed benign intracranial hypertension after 3 weeks of levofloxacin intake. The headache, diplopia, and papilledema resolved within a week after levofloxacin was withdrawn. Physicians must be aware that quinolone antibiotics can potentially cause intracranial hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
